      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "The marble has fallen perfectly for FINAL DEADLINE NZ (1). He has been too good in winning his two starts off a spell, the latest when he came from much wider but worked to the front before scoring by nearly 6m at Albion Park. Won the Redcliffe Gold Cup the only time he raced here and owns a strong third-up record so is hard to go past. ALWAYS B COOL NZ (2) is a progressive gelding yet to miss a place. Won fresh then worked from a tough draw last time but stuck on. Won his lone second-up attempt and draws well. DANCE WITH CARMER (7) brings some decent form from Menangle, placing behind Eureka hopeful The Last Trip last start. Draws to trail Final Deadline and is proven at this distance. FRENCH FRIES (6) draws wide but should be close to his peak after placing in both runs off a spell. GREASED LIGHTNIN NZ (3) is ticking along well and draws to be competitive.",
